(3888100, 541819, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Slow Joe''s 1932 Pontiac" is an interesting entry into the Burst of Color challenge.  <br/> <br/>At first glance I had to stop and look for a minute because the burst of color really doesn''t pop out off the page.  The composition is the most interesting thing in this piece.  I really like that neither wheel is actually complete.  The reflection captured is also nice and gives the piece good flow. <br/> <br/>Overall I think you have a never nice and interesting piece, I am just not sure it really displays a burst of color for most voters.   I really like this photograph it really made me stop and think.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Slow Joe''s 1932 Pontiac" is an interesting entry into the Burst of Color challenge.   At first glance I had to stop and look for a minute because the burst of color really doesn''t pop out off the page.  The composition is the most interesting thing in this piece.  I really like that neither wheel is actually complete.  The reflection captured is also nice and gives the piece good flow.  Overall I think you have a never nice and interesting piece, I am just not sure it really displays a burst of color for most voters.   I really like this photograph it really made me stop and think.', '2007-07-10 03:49:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3888108, 544253, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Mellow Yellow" is an nice entry into the Burst of Color challenge.  <br/> <br/>I think your subject is great, I like that are subjects are really lying on the thirds of the frame. I am not sure if the soft focus was intentional or maybe there was a breeze blowing by.  I think the movement does give your piece something interesting that draws the viewer in.  I wonder if you had just focused on one flowers specifically and let the rest melt into the background it would have scored a little higher.  <br/> <br/>Overall this is a nice piece the colors are nice, a little soft for a burst of color but I think it works well for this piece.  I really look forward to seeing more entries from you, best of luck!</td>', '*Critique Club* "Mellow Yellow" is an nice entry into the Burst of Color challenge.   I think your subject is great, I like that are subjects are really lying on the thirds of the frame. I am not sure if the soft focus was intentional or maybe there was a breeze blowing by.  I think the movement does give your piece something interesting that draws the viewer in.  I wonder if you had just focused on one flowers specifically and let the rest melt into the background it would have scored a little higher.   Overall this is a nice piece the colors are nice, a little soft for a burst of color but I think it works well for this piece.  I really look forward to seeing more entries from you, best of luck!', '2007-07-10 03:56:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3888116, 543700, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Dragon" is a good entry into the Burst of Color challenge.  <br/> <br/>I really like the subject you have found, you have really found a burst of color in every day life.  The subject is really enchanting and grabs my eye.  <br/> <br/>I would be curious to see the image if you kicked up the contrast a little more to bring out more color in the image.  Also I would be interested to see the Dragon placed on maybe the first third from the left to kind of off center the image.  <br/> <br/>Overall I think this is a very strong piece for the challenge and you have done a very nice job.  I look forward to your future challenges.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Dragon" is a good entry into the Burst of Color challenge.   I really like the subject you have found, you have really found a burst of color in every day life.  The subject is really enchanting and grabs my eye.   I would be curious to see the image if you kicked up the contrast a little more to bring out more color in the image.  Also I would be interested to see the Dragon placed on maybe the first third from the left to kind of off center the image.   Overall I think this is a very strong piece for the challenge and you have done a very nice job.  I look forward to your future challenges.', '2007-07-10 04:03:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3888133, 542892, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Plaza" is a nice entry into the Burst of Color challenge.  <br/> <br/>This is nice entry into the challenge, we can defiantly see the colors in the shot.  I like the balance of yellow, purple and green.  I am not quite sure if you meant for the image to have a soft focus, but I think it may have score a little higher if the focus was a little stronger.  <br/> <br/>The composition is good I might try to not center the subject as much maybe cut out a little more of the water.    Nice job on this photograph, I look forward to more of your challenges!</td>', '*Critique Club* "Plaza" is a nice entry into the Burst of Color challenge.   This is nice entry into the challenge, we can defiantly see the colors in the shot.  I like the balance of yellow, purple and green.  I am not quite sure if you meant for the image to have a soft focus, but I think it may have score a little higher if the focus was a little stronger.   The composition is good I might try to not center the subject as much maybe cut out a little more of the water.    Nice job on this photograph, I look forward to more of your challenges!', '2007-07-10 04:09:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3888333, 543015, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>The post processing of this image is wonderful and there is no doubt that this entry meets the challenge.  The subtle desaturation reflects upon your vast experience here at DPC.  <br/> <br/>Where this challenge entry misses the mark for me is two fold.  First, almost all of the people have their back to the camera.  There is no eye contact to help hold the viewers attention.  Second, there is no story here.  Obviously this is some sort of event but being from the other side of the pond, I have no clue as to what is going on or why these people are gathered together.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, The post processing of this image is wonderful and there is no doubt that this entry meets the challenge.  The subtle desaturation reflects upon your vast experience here at DPC.   Where this challenge entry misses the mark for me is two fold.  First, almost all of the people have their back to the camera.  There is no eye contact to help hold the viewers attention.  Second, there is no story here.  Obviously this is some sort of event but being from the other side of the pond, I have no clue as to what is going on or why these people are gathered together. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2007-07-10 08:36:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3888374, 542254, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>The post processing of this image is well done and there is no doubt that this entry meets the challenge.  Where this challenge entry misses the mark for me is two fold.  First, there really isn''t a main subject to help anchor this image besides the color.  As the viewer''s eyes move around the image there is nothing that holds their attention for any length of time.  Second, there are so many layers to this image, the flowers, the box, and the window, that it looks cluttered.  Another byproduct of not having a main subject in the composition.<br/> <br/>I''m glad I received this image to critique, as it gave me the opportunity to take another look at your portfolio.  I remember critiquing your Triptych II and I like the additions you''ve made to your portfolio since that critique.  Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, The post processing of this image is well done and there is no doubt that this entry meets the challenge.  Where this challenge entry misses the mark for me is two fold.  First, there really isn''t a main subject to help anchor this image besides the color.  As the viewer''s eyes move around the image there is nothing that holds their attention for any length of time.  Second, there are so many layers to this image, the flowers, the box, and the window, that it looks cluttered.  Another byproduct of not having a main subject in the composition. I''m glad I received this image to critique, as it gave me the opportunity to take another look at your portfolio.  I remember critiquing your Triptych II and I like the additions you''ve made to your portfolio since that critique.  Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2007-07-10 08:51:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3888829, 544195, 78114, '<td valign="top">i love the cropping of this image... the way the form fits in the frame. i also like the lighting. something very interesting and intriguing about this photo!</td>', 'i love the cropping of this image... the way the form fits in the frame. i also like the lighting. something very interesting and intriguing about this photo!', '2007-07-10 11:17:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3889217, 542750, 48471, '<td valign="top">I still like this photo, it has more emotion than thousands of flowers and sunsets, it''s human.</td>', 'I still like this photo, it has more emotion than thousands of flowers and sunsets, it''s human.', '2007-07-10 13:25:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3890462, 541800, 66515, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>Well, a lot of sung praise to your submission so there isn''t a lot I can say that hasn''t already been said. At best I may end up summarizing what previous comments have already said. <br/> <br/>Exposure: yes the skies are dark but that is quite effective here. It creates a nice ominous mood for the sky. It also helps create a strong contrast with the color of the life preserver. A light sky would weaken the effect considerably.<br/> <br/>Composition: Simple but effective. Good negative space on the left but its got enough detail for the eye to see something interesting. The diagonal lines on the lighthouse effectively take your eye into the picture. The position of the life preserver is excellent: in a strong position without overpowering the shot. <br/> <br/>Color: Great rich colors that are nicely saturated without going overboard. <br/> <br/>The Challenge: Definitely meets the challenge. At 4th place the voters agree too. <br/> <br/>Overall: Great image. Sadly DPC doesn''t give ribbons for 4th place because this shot deserves one.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Well, a lot of sung praise to your submission so there isn''t a lot I can say that hasn''t already been said. At best I may end up summarizing what previous comments have already said.  Exposure: yes the skies are dark but that is quite effective here. It creates a nice ominous mood for the sky. It also helps create a strong contrast with the color of the life preserver. A light sky would weaken the effect considerably. Composition: Simple but effective. Good negative space on the left but its got enough detail for the eye to see something interesting. The diagonal lines on the lighthouse effectively take your eye into the picture. The position of the life preserver is excellent: in a strong position without overpowering the shot.  Color: Great rich colors that are nicely saturated without going overboard.  The Challenge: Definitely meets the challenge. At 4th place the voters agree too.  Overall: Great image. Sadly DPC doesn''t give ribbons for 4th place because this shot deserves one.', '2007-07-10 19:49:04.000000', NULL, 0),
