(3983856, 542761, 44877, '<td valign="top">I kind of like this. Too bad it got slammed so badly. It does fit the challenge - a burst of color indeed. <br/> <br/>As an aside - and you probably know this - you don''t need a model release for street photography unless you''re going to use it to advertise for something or put it on the cover of a book. I find it annoying to think that some people voted you down on account of their misinformation.</td>', 'I kind of like this. Too bad it got slammed so badly. It does fit the challenge - a burst of color indeed.  As an aside - and you probably know this - you don''t need a model release for street photography unless you''re going to use it to advertise for something or put it on the cover of a book. I find it annoying to think that some people voted you down on account of their misinformation.', '2007-08-09 12:17:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3983922, 542761, 60862, '<td valign="top">Ha!  Maybe cropping tighter would have made the point better?  Like bringing the top all the way down so their heads are as far from the top as their feet are from the bottom.<br/> <br/>Also, I think a different title could help you answer emorgan49''s excellent questions.  Not every shot has to have a moral, but you increase the impact if it does.</td>', 'Ha!  Maybe cropping tighter would have made the point better?  Like bringing the top all the way down so their heads are as far from the top as their feet are from the bottom. Also, I think a different title could help you answer emorgan49''s excellent questions.  Not every shot has to have a moral, but you increase the impact if it does.', '2007-08-09 12:41:25.000000', NULL, 0),
